# False positives: empty placeholders in .env.example.
#
# The per-source input-bucket credentials are documented as empty (unset = the
# bucket is read anonymously). With no value after the `=`, the generic-api-key
# rule's whitespace class steps over the line break and captures the NEXT line's
# variable name as the "secret" — hence every finding spans two lines (L39-L40,
# L41-L42, ...) and only the ACCESS_KEY halves fire. The reported entropies
# (3.55-3.81) are those of a 24-char uppercase identifier, not of a real key.
#
# Verified: `git log --all -p -- .env.example` shows these keys have never held
# a value on any branch.
